            <p>
                Welcome to the ultimate guide to exploring Islamabad, where we uncover the popular places to visit in Islamabad and best picnic points. From its rich history to its stunning natural landscapes, Islamabad offers an unforgettable experience for travellers of all kinds.
               <br />
                Immerse yourself in the fascinating culture and heritage as you visit the iconic Faisal Mosque, the largest mosque in South Asia, or explore the grandeur of Pakistan Monument, representing unity and diversity. For nature enthusiasts, a visit to the picturesque Daman-e-Koh viewpoint is a must, offering breathtaking panoramic views of the city. Discover the beauty of Lake View Park, where you can indulge in outdoor activities such as boating, hiking, and picnicking amidst lush greenery and serene lakes. Explore the enchanting Lok Virsa Museum to delve deeper into Pakistan's rich cultural heritage and traditional arts. Don't miss out on the lively food scene in Islamabad, where you can savour delicious local delicacies and experience the bustling street food culture.
            </p>
